1
00:00:00,470 --> 00:00:02,040
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,110 --> 00:00:03,340
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,910 --> 00:00:08,250
(Episode 7)

5
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:15,990
Mom.

6
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,090
You're watching over me, right?

7
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:21,490
I'll never disappoint you again.

8
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:25,260
Even if the world locks me away,
I'll never give up.

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,630
Whoever took your life
and did this to me,

10
00:00:29,170 --> 00:00:31,240
I'll find them and make them pay.

11
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,370
So please, keep watching over me.

12
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:03,640
(Care With Sincerity,
Guide With Integrity)

13
00:01:23,790 --> 00:01:28,190
(5 years later)

14
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:45,610
(Korean Language)

15
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:52,150
(High School Equivalency Test
Score Report)

16
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:54,250
Is that even possible?

17
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,290
I see her in a different light now.

18
00:01:58,420 --> 00:01:59,690
(High School Equivalency Test
Score Report)

19
00:02:03,230 --> 00:02:07,030
(Year 2026)

20
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:17,110
Hey, that's enough. You can stop.

21
00:02:20,550 --> 00:02:22,480
Hey, my shoulders are next.

22
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:29,490
What the...
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

23
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,360
Why you...

24
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:32,590
Darn.

25
00:02:33,590 --> 00:02:34,590
What gives?

26
00:02:34,730 --> 00:02:35,990
We don't do violence here.

27
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:38,330
What?

28
00:02:39,130 --> 00:02:40,870
Hey, let go.

29
00:02:43,870 --> 00:02:45,800
Hey! Okay, I get it, so let go.

30
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:48,640
Darn it.

31
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:52,580
Thanks.

32
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:54,710
Inmate 2751, visitor.

33
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:57,620
I have good news.

34
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:00,250
Good news?

35
00:03:00,450 --> 00:03:03,090
- What...
- It's been a tough ten years.

36
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:06,190
Your parole was approved.

37
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,730
Parole?

38
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:10,360
Does that mean I'm getting out?

39
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,960
Yes, soon.

40
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:16,530
Thank you.
Thank you so much, Attorney Seo.

41
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:20,570
You don't have to thank me.
This was all you.

42
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,440
(Building
Advanced Constitutional State...)

43
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:26,440
(Where People Are Happy)

44
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:37,120
Eun Seol.

45
00:03:40,260 --> 00:03:42,960
Welcome back to the outside world.

46
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:44,860
Attorney Seo.

47
00:03:45,530 --> 00:03:46,630
You've been through a lot.

48
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,170
You're the reason
I was able to get through it.

49
00:03:50,570 --> 00:03:51,700
Thank you so much.

50
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,770
I'm the one
who should be thanking you.

51
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:55,310
You endured it all so well.

52
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:56,840
Let's go, then.

53
00:03:57,740 --> 00:03:58,740
Where to?

54
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:00,780
Eun Seol,
do you have anywhere to go?

55
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:02,680
No.

56
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:05,220
Then come with me.

57
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:07,690
Let me get that. Let's go.

58
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,340
Where are we?

59
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:35,850
It's my place. Let's go.

60
00:04:42,850 --> 00:04:43,860
Come on.

61
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:45,920
Sister, I'm home.

62
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:47,630
Why are you home so early?

63
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:50,700
Who's this?

64
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,600
This is Ko Eun Seol.

65
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:54,630
I told you
she was getting paroled today.

66
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:56,700
Say hello. This is my sister.

67
00:04:57,970 --> 00:04:59,070
Hello.

68
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:00,770
Yes, hello.

69
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:04,540
Teun Teun, say hello.
She's a friend of Uncle's.

70
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:07,550
Hello. I'm Seo Teun Teun.

71
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,050
Teun Teun, go to your room.

72
00:05:10,110 --> 00:05:11,120
Why, Mom?

73
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:13,450
- Go on, now.
- Okay.

74
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:18,020
Can I talk to you for a second?

75
00:05:21,430 --> 00:05:23,060
Please wait here a moment.

76
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:24,860
- Sure.
- All right.

77
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:39,380
What is it?

78
00:05:39,740 --> 00:05:41,450
What do you think you're doing?

79
00:05:41,650 --> 00:05:43,180
Wasn't she convicted of murder?

80
00:05:43,250 --> 00:05:45,850
Why would you invite her to stay
when we have Teun Teun here?

81
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:48,850
I told you, she was framed.

82
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:51,290
Even if she was framed...

83
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:53,060
She's still an ex-con.

84
00:05:53,830 --> 00:05:54,830
Come on, Mi Rae.

85
00:05:55,390 --> 00:05:58,730
Whatever. Just make an excuse
and get her out of here.

86
00:05:59,030 --> 00:06:00,700
Is this who you've always been?

87
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,970
Have you always been this heartless?

88
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,600
Hey, Seo Hyun Jae.

89
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:07,210
She just got out after ten years.

90
00:06:07,770 --> 00:06:11,310
Is it so wrong that I wanted her
to eat a good home-cooked meal?

91
00:06:13,110 --> 00:06:14,680
You could've at least
given me a heads-up.

92
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:16,810
I didn't know you'd react like this.

93
00:06:18,050 --> 00:06:19,180
I'm really disappointed.

94
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:25,090
Wait, where did she go?

95
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:28,730
Eun Seol, are you in the bathroom?

96
00:06:30,030 --> 00:06:31,030
What is it?

97
00:06:31,930 --> 00:06:32,930
Is she gone?

98
00:06:33,970 --> 00:06:35,430
She must've heard us.

99
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,300
Darn it.

100
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:47,650
Eun Seol!

101
00:06:49,210 --> 00:06:50,210
Wait a minute.

102
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:53,720
I'm so sorry.

103
00:06:54,850 --> 00:06:57,160
It's all right.
I understand how your sister feels.

104
00:06:57,860 --> 00:06:59,490
I probably would've done
the same thing.

105
00:07:00,930 --> 00:07:03,460
Please don't go.
Let's at least get something to eat.

106
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:06,560
I'm grateful enough
that you came to get me.

107
00:07:07,230 --> 00:07:08,870
From now on,
I'll try to make it on my own.

108
00:07:10,670 --> 00:07:11,840
But you said you have nowhere to go.

109
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:15,010
You probably don't have any money.
How will you manage?

110
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:18,340
I have some money
I earned doing prison work.

111
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:20,480
I should be able
to afford a small room.

112
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:23,280
Then let's at least
look for a room together, okay?

113
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:26,650
I'm heading to the columbarium
to see my mom now.

114
00:07:27,850 --> 00:07:29,850
I'll contact you
after I visit and get settled.

115
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,160
I mean it.

116
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:36,790
I have to find the real killer,

117
00:07:37,330 --> 00:07:39,330
and to do that,
I desperately need your help.

118
00:07:40,870 --> 00:07:44,000
Then you have to promise
you'll call me, okay?

119
00:07:44,570 --> 00:07:45,570
I will.

120
00:07:55,410 --> 00:07:56,780
Who was released?

121
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:58,280
Ko Eun Seol.

122
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:01,020
But she still had a lot of time left
on her sentence.

123
00:08:02,090 --> 00:08:04,460
She was granted parole
for model behavior.

124
00:08:05,290 --> 00:08:06,390
What the...

125
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,190
Parole?

126
00:08:08,930 --> 00:08:09,930
Yes.

127
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:15,200
How is Lee Jung Tae doing?
The guard from back then.

128
00:08:15,330 --> 00:08:18,700
Well, I haven't checked
on him since.

129
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:20,440
Find out.

130
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:21,810
Yes, ma'am.

131
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:24,280
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

132
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:42,830
(The late Park Hee Jung)

133
00:08:47,970 --> 00:08:48,970
Mom.

134
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:51,840
Have you been well?

135
00:08:59,110 --> 00:09:00,950
I still can't believe...

136
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:04,680
that you're not here
with me anymore.

137
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:11,220
What in the world happened that day?

138
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:17,060
Who did this to you, Mom?

139
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:19,860
(The late Park Hee Jung)

140
00:09:21,370 --> 00:09:22,500
Excuse me.

141
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:25,070
What was your relationship
to the deceased?

142
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:28,070
She was my mother.

143
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:29,670
Why do you ask?

144
00:09:29,810 --> 00:09:31,540
The maintenance fees
are five years behind,

145
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:33,210
so I came to empty the niche.

146
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,180
I only asked since you were here.

147
00:09:35,650 --> 00:09:37,210
For five years?

148
00:09:41,050 --> 00:09:43,020
How much are the back fees?

149
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,320
(Serving with Warmth and Integrity)

150
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,760
Excuse me, Officer.
We were asked to come down here.

151
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,460
Oh, Eun Guk.

152
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,800
Grandma,
you didn't have to come too.

153
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:57,840
What happened this time?
Did someone provoke you again?

154
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,070
Is that what happened?

155
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,240
How badly...

156
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,140
did you hurt them this time?

157
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:05,780
How much...

158
00:10:06,910 --> 00:10:08,350
will it take to settle this?

159
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,620
Don't settle.

160
00:10:13,850 --> 00:10:15,420
I can just do a little time
and get out.

161
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:18,160
You foolish boy.
How can you say something like that?

162
00:10:19,690 --> 00:10:20,690
So...

163
00:10:20,990 --> 00:10:22,430
where's the victim?

164
00:10:22,530 --> 00:10:24,360
He's at the hospital
receiving treatment.

165
00:10:26,930 --> 00:10:28,030
Eat this tofu.

166
00:10:28,470 --> 00:10:31,900
You're supposed to eat tofu
after getting out of police custody.

167
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:35,840
If eating tofu solved everything,
we wouldn't be in this mess.

168
00:10:36,270 --> 00:10:37,270
Did you already forget...

169
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:39,010
that his settlement money
cost us our house?

170
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:42,450
This is the last time.

171
00:10:42,950 --> 00:10:44,080
I won't pick any more fights.

172
00:10:44,180 --> 00:10:46,550
Talk all you want.
Like I'm going to believe you.

173
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:48,850
Come on.
What do you expect him to say?

174
00:10:49,790 --> 00:10:50,790
Stop laughing.

175
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,090
What's there to laugh about?

176
00:11:01,230 --> 00:11:03,430
(Mr. Ko Gi Han, Park Hee Jung's
columbarium fee was paid in full.)

177
00:11:05,370 --> 00:11:07,170
The columbarium maintenance fee
was paid in full?

178
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:12,080
- Was it you?
- What was?

179
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:14,280
Did you pay the maintenance fee
for the niche?

180
00:11:15,850 --> 00:11:16,850
No.

181
00:11:17,350 --> 00:11:19,050
Then, was it you, Mom?

182
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:22,620
Do I look like the kind of person
who would pay that?

183
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:25,920
If it wasn't Eun Guk or you,
then who paid it?

184
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:27,790
Give them a call.

185
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:36,130
Yes, hello. I'm calling about
a text message I just received.

186
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:39,200
Who paid the maintenance fee
for Park Hee Jung's niche?

187
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:42,870
Who?

188
00:11:43,670 --> 00:11:44,880
Ko Eun Seol?

189
00:12:03,860 --> 00:12:05,130
(Property Seizure Notice)

190
00:12:05,130 --> 00:12:07,530
(Creditor: Choi Moon Soo,
Debtor: Ko Gi Han)

191
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,200
What are you doing here?

192
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,400
Eun Guk.

193
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:15,340
Who says I'm your brother?

194
00:12:15,670 --> 00:12:17,110
Hey, what's wrong with you?

195
00:12:19,810 --> 00:12:22,480
When did you get out?
You should've called us.

196
00:12:22,510 --> 00:12:24,080
Call us? Over my dead body.

197
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:27,820
Didn't you know
you've been disowned?

198
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:31,360
Who do you think you are,
paying for my mom's memorial niche?

199
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:35,760
Before I start cursing you out,
just get lost.

200
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:39,860
If I see you one more time,

201
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,300
you're dead.

202
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,440
Him and that temper.

203
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:53,740
I didn't even come visit you.

204
00:12:54,810 --> 00:12:55,880
I'm sorry.

205
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:57,080
It's okay, Dad.

206
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,350
Are you out of your mind?

207
00:12:58,780 --> 00:13:00,990
Are you saying that
because you forgot what she did?

208
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:03,950
Eun Seol didn't do it, Mom.

209
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:05,160
If she didn't do it,

210
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:07,690
then why did she rot in prison
for ten years?

211
00:13:08,490 --> 00:13:10,430
- Well, that's...
- I don't want to hear it.

212
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:13,230
You. You heard what Eun Guk said.

213
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:16,330
Don't you ever come near here again.
Got it?

214
00:13:16,830 --> 00:13:19,470
- Let's go inside. Come on!
- Give me a second.

215
00:13:22,470 --> 00:13:23,470
I'm sorry.

216
00:13:23,770 --> 00:13:25,710
The family's just really overwhelmed
right now.

217
00:13:26,710 --> 00:13:28,880
Do you have a place to stay?

218
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:32,220
For now...

219
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:34,120
Take care of yourself, Eun Seol.

220
00:13:34,850 --> 00:13:37,320
My phone number hasn't changed,
so make sure you call me. Okay?

221
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:39,120
What are you doing? Get inside.

222
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:41,060
I'm sorry.

223
00:14:53,300 --> 00:14:55,530
Hello. Excuse me,
can I ask you something?

224
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:57,840
I'm looking for a Mr. Lee Jung Tae.
Is he here?

225
00:14:58,070 --> 00:14:59,100
Who?

226
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:02,440
There was a man named Lee Jung Tae
who worked here ten years ago.

227
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,440
Don't you know him?

228
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:05,080
You're looking for that guy too?

229
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:10,180
Wait, did someone else
come by looking for him?

230
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,620
A man was here just a moment ago.

231
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:15,090
He was looking for him.

232
00:15:15,090 --> 00:15:16,820
Just now? Who was it?

233
00:15:16,850 --> 00:15:18,260
I wouldn't know that.

234
00:15:21,690 --> 00:15:24,630
So is Lee Jung Tae
still working here?

235
00:15:24,630 --> 00:15:27,160
No, he quit a long time ago.

236
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:30,700
Hold on.
I heard he moved to Vietnam.

237
00:15:30,770 --> 00:15:31,770
Vietnam?

238
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:36,040
Then, do you have
his contact information?

239
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,410
I don't know him well.

240
00:15:38,010 --> 00:15:41,150
The part about him going to Vietnam?
That was just something I overheard.

241
00:15:42,910 --> 00:15:43,910
I see.

242
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:45,950
Thank you.

243
00:15:48,190 --> 00:15:49,220
Take care.

244
00:15:55,230 --> 00:15:56,930
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

245
00:16:08,370 --> 00:16:09,370
Eun Seol.

246
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:11,740
Yes.

247
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:13,510
Sure thing.

248
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:15,110
I'll see you later then.

249
00:16:22,490 --> 00:16:23,520
Vietnam?

250
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:26,320
He quit his security job
a long time ago...

251
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:29,260
and has been living in Vietnam
for the past few years.

252
00:16:32,130 --> 00:16:33,130
All right.

253
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:35,200
What do you have there?

254
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:38,740
It's the proposal
for the 50th anniversary celebration...

255
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:40,640
from the planning team at HQ.

256
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:43,340
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

257
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:45,980
Hold on.

258
00:16:47,610 --> 00:16:49,750
If it's from HQ's planning team,

259
00:16:51,150 --> 00:16:52,680
does that mean
Chief Choi's leading this?

260
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:54,120
Yes, ma'am.

261
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:07,730
If he's in Vietnam,
finding him won't be easy.

262
00:17:08,370 --> 00:17:10,000
Not unless we have
his contact information.

263
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:12,800
Still, we have to find him
no matter what.

264
00:17:13,970 --> 00:17:15,710
Did he have any family?

265
00:17:16,910 --> 00:17:20,040
Well, I believe he was divorced
at the time.

266
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:23,580
Oh, right. He did have a mother.

267
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:25,280
- His mother?
- Yes.

268
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,980
Then please look for her.

269
00:17:28,050 --> 00:17:29,050
I will.

270
00:17:29,850 --> 00:17:31,020
Also...

271
00:17:31,860 --> 00:17:33,590
There's something
that's bothering me.

272
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:35,160
What is it?

273
00:17:35,230 --> 00:17:38,630
Someone else was there earlier
looking for Lee Jung Tae.

274
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,170
And the guard seemed to be
hiding something, reluctant to talk.

275
00:17:42,970 --> 00:17:43,970
Really?

276
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:51,610
Could it be...

277
00:17:51,910 --> 00:17:55,010
the person who paid Lee Jung Tae
to commit perjury?

278
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:58,220
We have to hurry.

279
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:00,580
Right.

280
00:18:03,350 --> 00:18:05,460
Revise the entire proposal
for the anniversary event?

281
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:06,990
That's just ridiculous.

282
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:10,660
A seven-star hotel,
VIP guests, and so on.

283
00:18:10,830 --> 00:18:13,360
It doesn't align with the company's
founding principles at all.

284
00:18:14,230 --> 00:18:15,570
It's the 50th anniversary.
We should go all out.

285
00:18:15,570 --> 00:18:16,670
Chief Choi.

286
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,040
So,

287
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:21,910
do you have an alternative?

288
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:25,140
Yes, I've prepared one.

289
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:32,050
(Cheongma Group's
50th Anniversary Celebration)

290
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:43,730
(Lowering Barriers,
Filling Lives With Warmth)

291
00:18:43,730 --> 00:18:47,000
Our founder's philosophy was not
to judge people by their clothes,

292
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,670
but to break down barriers
through fashion.

293
00:18:49,430 --> 00:18:52,840
That's why the profits were donated
to the scholarship foundation,

294
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:54,270
making it the largest shareholder.

295
00:18:55,840 --> 00:18:58,280
"Lowering barriers,
filling lives with warmth."

296
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:01,280
To honor the spirit
of our 50th anniversary,

297
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:04,250
the event will be held
in the company auditorium.

298
00:19:04,550 --> 00:19:05,780
The company auditorium?

299
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:07,120
You can't be serious.

300
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:09,450
In a location
that best embodies Cheongma,

301
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:12,220
we'll show we're getting back
to our roots.

302
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:14,260
If getting back to our roots
cheapens the brand,

303
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:15,690
who will take responsibility?

304
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:19,800
It seems you don't realize
now is the time for a premium strategy.

305
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:21,470
Continue, Director Joo.

306
00:19:22,170 --> 00:19:23,170
Madam Chairman.

307
00:19:23,770 --> 00:19:25,240
Let's hear her out.

308
00:19:26,470 --> 00:19:28,110
(Don't Discriminate by Clothes)

309
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:34,340
The main event will be a runway show
featuring our customers.

310
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:36,610
We'll put customers on the stage,

311
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:40,050
and children will join Madam Chairman
for the finale.

312
00:19:40,350 --> 00:19:41,990
This is a prime opportunity...

313
00:19:42,050 --> 00:19:43,520
to cement her position...

314
00:19:43,590 --> 00:19:46,190
as the foundation's chair,
rather than just an actress.

315
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:51,630
Me, in the finale?

316
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:54,230
Instead of the children,

317
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:56,170
what if I walked the runway
with Mom?

318
00:19:56,430 --> 00:19:58,440
Perhaps another time,
Team Leader Kang.

319
00:19:58,970 --> 00:20:00,070
Why?

320
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:09,550
Fine.

321
00:20:09,950 --> 00:20:12,280
I'd feel a bit awkward,

322
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:15,390
but the idea itself
sounds fresh and good.

323
00:20:16,290 --> 00:20:17,960
What does everyone else think?

324
00:20:23,390 --> 00:20:24,800
Please tell her
you're against it, sir.

325
00:20:25,130 --> 00:20:26,930
The event's too centered
around Madam Chairman.

326
00:20:27,230 --> 00:20:29,270
I don't really have grounds
to object,

327
00:20:29,330 --> 00:20:31,000
so I'll be generous and let it pass.

328
00:20:31,340 --> 00:20:33,870
Taking one step back
to take two steps forward.

329
00:20:34,470 --> 00:20:35,470
But sir...

330
00:20:35,770 --> 00:20:37,070
That's enough.

331
00:20:37,410 --> 00:20:39,440
My wife is in the palm of my hand,

332
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:40,910
so what's there to worry about?

333
00:20:40,910 --> 00:20:42,950
We'll just let her have her moment.

334
00:20:44,110 --> 00:20:45,380
By the way, Chief Choi,

335
00:20:46,650 --> 00:20:48,150
you're going to have to step it up.

336
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,990
Losing to Director Joo is
pretty embarrassing, if you ask me.

337
00:20:54,090 --> 00:20:57,490
Do we really need to build up
Madam Chairman that much?

338
00:20:58,930 --> 00:21:00,930
Why are you being so short-sighted?

339
00:21:01,330 --> 00:21:04,600
I'm not building her up.
I'm pulling her over to my side.

340
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:08,640
Won't that give
Madam Chairman the impression...

341
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:09,970
that I'm on hers?

342
00:21:10,170 --> 00:21:11,880
Right, I see.

343
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:15,280
Director Joo, a word.

344
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:18,350
- Manager Na, leave us.
- Yes, ma'am.

345
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:21,390
What are you playing at?

346
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:22,650
What do you mean?

347
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:24,550
What do you hope to gain
by going this far?

348
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:27,060
You're the one being strange,
Chief Choi.

349
00:21:27,060 --> 00:21:28,530
Why are you getting so worked up?

350
00:21:29,430 --> 00:21:31,290
Do you have some ulterior motive?

351
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,600
Don't make baseless accusations.

352
00:21:35,730 --> 00:21:37,070
Cheongma's founding anniversary?

353
00:21:37,470 --> 00:21:38,840
Getting back to Cheongma's roots?

354
00:21:40,270 --> 00:21:43,140
Since when have you ever cared
about that enough to propose it?

355
00:21:43,740 --> 00:21:45,480
What are you trying to say?

356
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:49,110
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

357
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:51,780
You've got some nerve, considering
you've only been at this...

358
00:21:51,780 --> 00:21:53,150
for a few years.

359
00:21:53,650 --> 00:21:55,420
What? An opportunity?

360
00:21:56,490 --> 00:21:58,690
Don't overstep your bounds
and stay humble.

361
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:01,060
Cheongma's roots, you say?

362
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:04,700
Don't forget you started out
as a nanny, Director Joo.

363
00:22:52,880 --> 00:22:56,550
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

364
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:01,790
Aren't you leaving yet, Ms. Kang?

365
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:03,450
I guess I should.

366
00:23:06,390 --> 00:23:08,930
Then, is it okay if we leave first?

367
00:23:09,790 --> 00:23:12,130
Wait a second.
Let me just finish uploading this.

368
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:14,160
It's scary being here all by myself.

369
00:23:14,530 --> 00:23:16,200
Right. Of course.

370
00:23:17,830 --> 00:23:19,070
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

371
00:23:19,140 --> 00:23:20,970
Actually, you guys go on home.

372
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:24,110
- See you tomorrow, then.
- See you tomorrow.

373
00:23:27,210 --> 00:23:28,650
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

374
00:23:28,710 --> 00:23:31,250
Seok Jin, it's unlike you to call
at this hour.

375
00:23:31,380 --> 00:23:32,580
Isn't it the middle of the night
over there?

376
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:35,990
Who approved the new product line?

377
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:38,320
Who do you think? I did.

378
00:23:38,860 --> 00:23:39,860
Why do you ask?

379
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:44,060
The reaction here has been terrible.

380
00:23:44,290 --> 00:23:46,330
We're receiving endless complaints
that prices went up...

381
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:48,000
for the same quality of clothing.

382
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,870
Isn't that expected
with production costs going up?

383
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:53,640
It's supposed to be a premium line,

384
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:55,910
so how can the quality be the same?

385
00:23:57,110 --> 00:23:58,380
Discontinue this line immediately.

386
00:23:58,880 --> 00:23:59,940
That's ridiculous.

387
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:02,180
This is my first launch
as team leader,

388
00:24:02,180 --> 00:24:03,450
and you're telling me to pull it?

389
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:05,350
Is that what's important right now?

390
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:07,180
Yes, it is to me.

391
00:24:07,980 --> 00:24:09,850
If that's all you have to say,
then I'm hanging up.

392
00:24:11,350 --> 00:24:12,760
Team Leader Kang. Kang Hae Ra!

393
00:24:14,260 --> 00:24:16,490
I thought he'd have
something better to say.

394
00:24:44,550 --> 00:24:45,820
Gosh. Ma'am!

395
00:24:48,190 --> 00:24:49,430
Ma'am, are you okay?

396
00:24:50,660 --> 00:24:52,200
Ma'am, are you okay?

397
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:54,660
I'll call 911.

398
00:24:54,730 --> 00:24:58,840
Gosh, I'm okay.
There's no need for 911.

399
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:01,740
- Oh, my.
- Are you sure you're okay?

400
00:25:03,740 --> 00:25:05,880
Here, let me help you get up.

401
00:25:06,010 --> 00:25:07,410
I'll walk you home.

402
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:09,710
Oh, dear.

403
00:25:20,660 --> 00:25:21,660
Goodness.

404
00:25:27,100 --> 00:25:29,670
Oh, dear. Thank you.

405
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:33,000
You still look so pale.

406
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:35,340
Are you sure
you don't need to see a doctor?

407
00:25:35,610 --> 00:25:39,440
The heat got to me,
and I felt dizzy for a second.

408
00:25:39,510 --> 00:25:42,180
I'll be fine
once I get some rest at home.

409
00:25:44,920 --> 00:25:47,650
It's a little warm in here.
Do you have any ice in the freezer?

410
00:25:48,550 --> 00:25:50,520
I do, but...

411
00:25:51,250 --> 00:25:52,290
Stay right there.

412
00:25:59,260 --> 00:26:03,530
That feels nice and cool.
I feel like I can breathe again.

413
00:26:03,770 --> 00:26:07,100
Let me do that.
I can hold it myself.

414
00:26:07,100 --> 00:26:08,310
Just try and relax.

415
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:11,310
I just feel like
I'm imposing on you.

416
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:13,310
- It's okay.
- Goodness.

417
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:15,210
That feels much better.

418
00:26:17,980 --> 00:26:18,980
I see.

419
00:26:20,150 --> 00:26:22,150
So how bad is it?

420
00:26:25,690 --> 00:26:26,690
All right.

421
00:26:26,860 --> 00:26:28,660
I'll set up
a video conference tomorrow,

422
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:30,030
so you can explain it yourself.

423
00:26:32,830 --> 00:26:34,560
What's so serious?

424
00:26:35,470 --> 00:26:36,800
Is Hae Ra not back yet?

425
00:26:37,070 --> 00:26:39,140
She should be home soon.
Here she comes now.

426
00:26:41,070 --> 00:26:43,140
What is it? Were you waiting for me?

427
00:26:43,740 --> 00:26:45,580
I made you team leader...

428
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:47,840
because you were so sure
you could handle it,

429
00:26:47,910 --> 00:26:50,450
and all you have to show for it
is a 40 percent drop in sales?

430
00:26:51,450 --> 00:26:52,920
Did you talk to Seok Jin?

431
00:26:53,850 --> 00:26:57,050
That's only the US market.
It isn't that bad in Korea.

432
00:26:57,120 --> 00:27:00,290
Is that really
all you have to say right now?

433
00:27:00,860 --> 00:27:03,060
If you don't think you're up to it,
leave the company...

434
00:27:03,260 --> 00:27:04,290
and just get married.

435
00:27:04,860 --> 00:27:06,430
- Unbelievable.
- Dad!

436
00:27:07,460 --> 00:27:09,400
Would it have killed you
to do better?

437
00:27:11,600 --> 00:27:13,370
It's not like I chose to fail,
you know.

438
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:18,340
Maybe I can use this to get them
to set up my marriage to Seok Jin.

439
00:27:20,840 --> 00:27:22,410
You don't feel confident?

440
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:25,820
Like confidence is all it takes
to get results.

441
00:27:42,870 --> 00:27:44,670
It really won't light today.

442
00:27:50,310 --> 00:27:53,710
Hey, Sang Beom. Long time no see.
Have you been well?

443
00:27:54,880 --> 00:27:55,880
Right.

444
00:27:56,650 --> 00:27:58,010
Someone came by looking for me?

445
00:27:59,880 --> 00:28:00,950
A young woman?

446
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:25,580
This really wasn't necessary.

447
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:27,840
Oh, nonsense.

448
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:31,350
I feel terrible
that this is all I can offer you.

449
00:28:31,350 --> 00:28:32,480
Please, drink up.

450
00:28:32,950 --> 00:28:35,190
I see. Thank you, ma'am.

451
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:43,330
By the way,
it seems like you live by yourself.

452
00:28:43,390 --> 00:28:45,260
I guess you can say that.

453
00:28:46,560 --> 00:28:49,000
- Then who's that in the photo?
- What?

454
00:28:50,330 --> 00:28:52,440
Oh, that's my son.

455
00:28:53,040 --> 00:28:55,710
He's doing business
in Vietnam right now.

456
00:28:57,570 --> 00:29:00,280
Come to think of it,
I haven't seen him in a while.

457
00:29:01,380 --> 00:29:04,310
I guess your son
doesn't drop by Korea often.

458
00:29:04,580 --> 00:29:06,150
Well, he's busy with work.

459
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:07,920
I see.

460
00:29:09,620 --> 00:29:11,620
So where in Vietnam is he?

461
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:14,120
Where did he say he was again?

462
00:29:14,720 --> 00:29:16,760
He said it was Dal-something.

463
00:29:17,360 --> 00:29:18,760
Dal-something?

464
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:22,500
I really can't remember.
Anyway, why do you ask?

465
00:29:23,830 --> 00:29:25,840
No reason. I was just asking.

466
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:28,270
- Well, I should get going.
- Sure.

467
00:29:28,470 --> 00:29:31,270
Oh, speak of the devil.

468
00:29:32,410 --> 00:29:34,380
Goodness. Jung Tae, is that you?

469
00:29:35,350 --> 00:29:37,550
Yes, it's Mom.

470
00:30:11,150 --> 00:30:14,850
(A Trap Called Desire)

471
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:16,490
This time, we'll catch them.

472
00:30:16,490 --> 00:30:19,390
We'll get the real killer
and clear your name.

473
00:30:19,620 --> 00:30:23,060
It really wasn't me.
How could I do something like that?

474
00:30:23,130 --> 00:30:24,690
The law found you guilty.

475
00:30:24,690 --> 00:30:26,660
And I'm telling you it wasn't me!

476
00:30:27,300 --> 00:30:29,970
Now I won't have to see
that irritating face anymore.

477
00:30:30,030 --> 00:30:31,630
- Nice one, Ms. Joo.
- I just want you...

478
00:30:31,630 --> 00:30:34,000
to inherit Cheongma.

479
00:30:34,100 --> 00:30:37,540
My whole life, I've always
gotten everything I wanted.

480
00:30:37,740 --> 00:30:40,510
But Seok Jin
has never once been mine.

481
00:30:41,040 --> 00:30:42,450
That's why I can't let him go.

482
00:30:43,080 --> 00:30:45,080
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
